RREEGGUULLAARR EEXXPPRREESSSSIIOONNSS
     The patterns used in addresses and in the ss command are
     regular expressions built from:

     cc       An ordinary character matches itself.

     .       Matches any single character.

     *       Matches zero or more occurrences of the single
             preceding character (or of a preceding ., [...], or
             \(...\)).

     ^       At the start of a pattern, anchors the match to the
             beginning of the pattern space.

     $       At the end of a pattern, anchors the match to the
             end of the pattern space.

     [_c_h_a_r_s], [^_c_h_a_r_s]


